  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Win the ball back in the middle zone",
  "description": "A full rink with a goalkeeper in each goal and 4 v 4 up to 6 v 6 outfield. Mark the middle zone with cones by the boards, about a third of the rink. All outfield players stay in the middle zone.\n\nBlue always start with a throw-out from their goalkeeper and must keep the ball within the team in the zone. Red try to win it. Once red have won the ball they need five passes in the zone – then they may leave it and attack blue's goal. Blue must win the ball back before red get there. Offside applies once red have left the zone.\n\nSwap roles after a few attacks. Harder for red: blue may defend over the whole rink even after red have left the zone, and red may counter straight after winning the ball with no passes needed. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "When you lose the ball: go at it right away, before the opponents can turn."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Stay close together when you have the ball – then you are already close when it is lost."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "The goalkeeper steps up in the penalty area, catches long balls and throws out quickly."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Red: play the first pass after winning the ball away from pressure, and create space between you."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
